{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"513f17ea0c678623","name":"card_unit_tropic_lightning","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_tropic_lightning","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"TROPIC LIGHTNING","text":"Draw a card the first time you gain an extra kredit slot. Your units get +2+2 the second time. Becomes Veteran the third time.","flavorText":"The 25th Infantry Division, nicknamed “Tropic Lightning”, was activated at Schofield Barracks in Hawaii in 1941. It was formed from Hawaiian garrison units just over two months before the attack on Pearl Harbor. After the Japanese air attack, the division moved into defensive positions around Honolulu and Ewa Point, then spent much of 1942 training for combat in the Pacific. The division entered battle on Guadalcanal in late 1942, relieving Marines near Henderson Field. In January 1943, it fought in the Mount Austen area and helped reduce the Japanese pocket there. Its advance toward Cape Esperance ended organized Japanese resistance on the island by February. Tropic Lightning soldiers next fought in the New Georgia campaign, where they moved through jungle and mud toward Bairoko Harbor and helped secure key islands in the central Solomons. After resting and training in New Zealand and New Caledonia, the division returned to combat on Luzon in the Philippines in 1945. It fought across the Central Plain, through the Caraballo Mountains, and captured Balete Pass, opening the route toward the Cagayan Valley.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":5,"operationCost":1,"attack":6,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_tropic_lightning","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_tropic_lightning_title","SourceString":"TROPIC LIGHTNING","LocalizedString":"TROPIC LIGHTNING"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":6,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_tropic_lightning_text","SourceString":"Draw a card the first time you gain an extra kredit slot. Your units get +2+2 the second time. Becomes Veteran the third time.","LocalizedString":"Draw a card the first time you gain an extra kredit slot. Your units get +2+2 the second time. Becomes Veteran the third time."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_tropic_lightning_history","SourceString":"The 25th Infantry Division, nicknamed “Tropic Lightning”, was activated at Schofield Barracks in Hawaii in 1941. It was formed from Hawaiian garrison units just over two months before the attack on Pearl Harbor. After the Japanese air attack, the division moved into defensive positions around Honolulu and Ewa Point, then spent much of 1942 training for combat in the Pacific. The division entered battle on Guadalcanal in late 1942, relieving Marines near Henderson Field. In January 1943, it fought in the Mount Austen area and helped reduce the Japanese pocket there. Its advance toward Cape Esperance ended organized Japanese resistance on the island by February. Tropic Lightning soldiers next fought in the New Georgia campaign, where they moved through jungle and mud toward Bairoko Harbor and helped secure key islands in the central Solomons. After resting and training in New Zealand and New Caledonia, the division returned to combat on Luzon in the Philippines in 1945. It fought across the Central Plain, through the Caraballo Mountains, and captured Balete Pass, opening the route toward the Cagayan Valley.","LocalizedString":"The 25th Infantry Division, nicknamed “Tropic Lightning”, was activated at Schofield Barracks in Hawaii in 1941. It was formed from Hawaiian garrison units just over two months before the attack on Pearl Harbor. After the Japanese air attack, the division moved into defensive positions around Honolulu and Ewa Point, then spent much of 1942 training for combat in the Pacific. The division entered battle on Guadalcanal in late 1942, relieving Marines near Henderson Field. In January 1943, it fought in the Mount Austen area and helped reduce the Japanese pocket there. Its advance toward Cape Esperance ended organized Japanese resistance on the island by February. Tropic Lightning soldiers next fought in the New Georgia campaign, where they moved through jungle and mud toward Bairoko Harbor and helped secure key islands in the central Solomons. After resting and training in New Zealand and New Caledonia, the division returned to combat on Luzon in the Philippines in 1945. It fought across the Central Plain, through the Caraballo Mountains, and captured Balete Pass, opening the route toward the Cagayan Valley."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_tropic_lightning_vet","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/TROPIC_LIGHTNING.TROPIC_LIGHTNING","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":341.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_tropic_lightning_photo","SourceString":"25th Infantry Division troops burning out a Japanese pillbox at Baguio in the Philippines, 1945.","LocalizedString":"25th Infantry Division troops burning out a Japanese pillbox at Baguio in the Philippines, 1945."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryL.47"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeHeavy_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeHeavy.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"isDirectDamage":true,"threat_level":0.2},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_tropic_lightning","owner":"card_unit_tropic_lig